{"ts": "2026-03-17T17:08:37.169285Z", "level": "info", "source": "backend", "category": "chatbot", "message": "Chatbot exchange", "data": {"question": "can u tell mw what is http error", "answer": "Of course! An HTTP (Hypertext Transfer Protocol) error occurs when there is a problem with the communication between your device and the server that hosts the website or web application you are trying to access. This could be due to several reasons such as network issues, server problems, incorrect URL, or other technical issues.\n\nHTTP errors are categorized based on their status code, which is a three-digit number that tells the client (like your browser) the result of the request made to the server. Common HTTP error codes include:\n\n1xx - Informational responses: The request was received and is being processed. There is no error with this status code.\n\n2xx - Successful responses: The server successfully processed the request. \n\n3xx - Redirection messages: Further action needs to be taken by the client. This could include moving to a different page on the same domain.\n\n4xx - Client errors: There is an error with the request sent from the client. Common examples are \"401 Unauthorized\" or \"404 Not Found\".\n\n5xx - Server errors: There is an error with the server that prevented it from fulfilling the request made by the client. Examples include \"500 Internal Server Error\" or \"503 Service Temporarily Unavailable\".\n\nIf you are experiencing an HTTP error, you might want to check your network connection, refresh the page, clear your browser cache, or contact the website owner if it's a persistent issue."}}
