{"ts": "2026-03-27T05:44:11.148461Z", "level": "info", "source": "backend", "category": "chatbot", "message": "Chatbot exchange", "data": {"question": "what are you", "answer": "I am AURA, an AI assistant for an ESP32-based autonomous rover and surveillance project. My system includes an ESP32 rover board for movement and sensors (gas, flame, ultrasonic, edge), an ESP32-CAM board for live video and face recognition, a FastAPI backend, a React dashboard (manual, patrol, analytics, people, Telegram pages) and a Telegram bot for alerts."}}
{"ts": "2026-03-27T05:46:11.915997Z", "level": "info", "source": "backend", "category": "chatbot", "message": "Chatbot exchange", "data": {"question": "how ti add face in face recoginition", "answer": "To add a face to the face recognition system, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Prepare the Image**: You need a high-quality image of the person whose face you want to add to the system. Make sure the image is clear and well-lit so that the system can accurately recognize it.\n\n2. **Upload the Image**: Log in to your dashboard or use the Telegram bot to upload the image you prepared. The interface should have a button or link for this purpose.\n\n3. **Adding the Face**: After uploading, there will be an option to add the face. This might involve labeling the image with the person's name, age, or any other relevant information.\n\n4. **Verify and Confirm**: Before saving the new entry, you may need to verify that the face in the image matches the name and details you have provided. Once you are satisfied, confirm the action to add the face to the system.\n\n5. **Check the Status**: After adding the face, you can check the status of the addition process to ensure it has been successfully added to the system. You can also verify that the system is functioning correctly by using the live video feed and facial recognition features.\n\nIf you encounter any issues or have further questions, feel free to ask!"}}
